0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
54. 701.8899999999999864 Td
(Discourse markers \(DMs\) constitute an indispensable linguistic mechanism in human communication,) Tj
T* (functioning as structural brackets that manage information exchange and interpersonal alignment. In English) Tj
T* (linguistics, items such as well, you know, I mean, actually, and anyway have transitioned from being viewed) Tj
T* (as stylistic filler words to recognized pragmatic devices that guide conversational processing.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
54. 629.8899999999999864 Td
(Schiffrin \(1987\) established that discourse markers operate across multiple planes of talk, including exchange) Tj
T* (structures, action structures, idea structures, and participation frameworks. Within second language \(L2\)) Tj
T* (academic environments, the mastery of these pragmatic markers reflects a learner communicative competence) Tj
T* (and fluency in negotiating meaning during collaborative dialogue.) Tj
ET
BT
/F10 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
54. 553.8899999999999864 Td
(1.2 Statement of the Problem) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
54. 533.8899999999999864 Td
(Despite extensive theoretical research into discourse markers within native speaker corpora, empirical) Tj
T* (investigations focusing on Pakistani ESL tertiary learners remain scarce. L2 speakers often encounter) Tj
T* (challenges in employing discourse markers appropriately, resulting in conversational breakdown, abrupt topic) Tj
T* (shifts, or unintended pragmalinguistic infelicities during academic discourse.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
