(2.1 Conceptual Definition of Discourse Markers) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
54. 701.8899999999999864 Td
(Discourse markers are sequentially dependent elements which bracket units of talk and convey procedural) Tj
T* (rather than conceptual meaning. Fraser \(1999\) classifies discourse markers into contrastive, elaborative,) Tj
T* (inferential, and temporal categories, asserting that their core role is to establish a pragmatic relationship) Tj
T* (between the host utterance and prior discourse context.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
54. 626.8899999999999864 Td
(Unlike content words, discourse markers do not alter the propositional truth value of a clause. For example,) Tj
T* (omitting the marker well in an answer does not change the factual content of the response, yet it eliminates) Tj
T* (vital metacommunicative cues signaling conversational hesitancy or prospective disagreement.) Tj
ET
BT
/F10 12 Tf
13.7999999999999989 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
54. 561.8899999999999864 Td
(2.2 Pragmatic Frameworks: Schiffrin and Fraser) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
54. 541.8899999999999864 Td
(Schiffrin \(1987\) seminal coherence model posits that discourse markers index utterances to both the speaker) Tj
T* (and the listener across simultaneous communicative planes. In this model, markers like you know invite) Tj
T* (addressee alignment, while I mean acts as an internal repair token signaling self-correction.) Tj
ET
BT
/F9 11 Tf
12.6499999999999986 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
